    <md:title>3.1.2: Self Check</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a9c219a7-ae37-44df-a2d7-df97abf3f8a7</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para dir="ltr">The plot below is a scatter plot of mean temperature in July and mean inches of rain per year for a sample of midwestern cities. A line is drawn to fit the data. </para>
      <para dir="ltr">
        <figure>
          <media alt="A SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS MEAN TEMPERATURE IN JULY IN DEGREES FAHRENHEIT ON THE X-AXIS AND MEAN RAINFALL PER YEAR IN INCHES ON THE Y-AXIS. THE LINE DRAWN INCREASES FROM LEFT TO RIGHT.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_03_04_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
      </para>
      <para dir="ltr">Use the line provided to predict the mean number of inches of rain per year for a city that has a mean temperature of 70°F in July. </para>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
